RSVP
====

Purpose
-------
Records a non-host user's request to attend a meeting and the current outcome.

Fields
------
- Id: Generated integer primary key
- User: User.Id (foreign key to the requesting user)
- Meeting: Meeting.Id (foreign key to the requested meeting)
- Request status: Current state of the request (working values: pending, approved, declined, cancelled, revoked; storage type TBD)
- Attendance mark: Unset unless the host marks that the approved attendee showed up (representation TBD)
- Request time: Whether to record this is TBD
- Latest host-decision time: Whether to record this is TBD

Relationships and behavior
--------------------------
- An RSVP refers to one non-host user and one meeting.
- A user may have only one current RSVP for a meeting at a time; the User and Meeting pair must be unique.
- A new request is pending until the host approves or declines it.
- If the host declines a request, the user may submit another request later.
- A user may cancel a pending request or approved RSVP any time before the meeting. Canceling an approved RSVP frees the spot.
- The host may revoke an approved RSVP; the spot becomes available for another request.
- Approved RSVPs count toward the meeting's capacity; pending requests do not.
- Only the current RSVP state is kept. A later request updates the same RSVP, and prior request attempts are not retained.
- After the meeting, the host marks only the approved attendees who showed up; other approved attendees remain unmarked.
- Attendance is not a measure of whether a user is safe.
